      "content": "Hey, I'm a high school history teacher putting together a unit on the era of New Imperialism. I want to do a debate-style activity where students have to see the world through the eyes of different people from that time. Can you write a persuasive essay from the perspective of a British colonial administrator in Africa around 1885? I need it to sound authentic to the period, specifically justifying why the imperial presence is actually beneficial for the local populations through the concept of the \"civilizing mission.\" Thanks!",
